# CITATION.cff — place this file in the root of the repository (next to README and LICENSE).
# GitHub reads it for the "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
# Lines starting with "#" are comments and are ignored.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  Please also cite the accompanying article (listed under "references")
  once it is published.
type: software
title: "Analysis code for: Determinants of FEV1 decline in cystic fibrosis in South Africa: a longitudinal cohort"
abstract: >-
  R code for the analyses reported in "Determinants of FEV1 decline in cystic
  fibrosis in South Africa: a longitudinal cohort", a study of the South African
  Cystic Fibrosis Registry (manuscript under revision at the Journal of Cystic
  Fibrosis). The repository holds 21 R scripts in run order - data preparation,
  linear mixed-effects models of FEV1 percent predicted, CFTR-modulator and
  event-anchored infection and exacerbation models, sensitivity analyses, table
  and figure generation, and QA scripts - together with a run_all.sh driver, a
  README describing what each script produces and where it appears in the
  manuscript, and an R session record (R 4.5.2; lme4, lmerTest, performance).
  Registry data are not included: they contain patient-level health information
  and are available on reasonable request from the South African Cystic Fibrosis
  Registry steering committee. With the registry file in place, the pipeline
  reproduces all reported outputs.
